;; PAIR-PROJ-LET-1. The sort cell, and it is NOT about free symbols.
;;
;; The second component is an ADMISSIBLE PAYLOAD SUM. `typeToSortA` lowers it to
;; the native `(Pair2 int Box)`; the alias-unaware `typeToSort` collapses Box to
;; int and gives `(Pair2 int int)`. The RESULT binder and `qualSortMap` have used
;; the alias-aware function since PAIR-RET, so a param binder built with the
;; other one would put two sorts on one type in one file. liquid-fixpoint answers
;; that with `Elaborate fails on v == pair2_1 s`, a SORT error and not a
;; free-symbol error.
;;
;; This cell fails if `emitParamBind` ever takes the alias-unaware sort for a
;; pair. It does not test the guard.
(export take-first)
(type Box (| Full int) (| Empty))
(def-shell take-first [s: (int, Box)] -> int
  (post (>= result 0))
  (let [(n (first s))]
    (if (>= n 0) n 0)))
